WHAT IS TRANSLATED, AND WHAT WAS DONE TO IT

warren-snail answers as PostgreSQL does, so where PostgreSQL's own steps define the answer, its C
source (releases 18.6 and 19 RC1) was translated into Rust, its steps kept in their order. Everywhere
below, the nature of the modification is the same: the code is translated from C into Rust; memory
and errors are Rust's (an error returned by value in PostgreSQL's words, where the C raises it);
values cross in the crate's own forms (a date as days from 1970, a jsonb as its text); PostgreSQL's
page layouts, memory contexts and catalog lookups are left out; and only the settings the snail
answers under are read (DateStyle ISO, MDY; IntervalStyle postgres; TimeZone UTC unless the feature
`zones` is on; lc_numeric and lc_time C). What differs from that is said beside the file.

